  "data": {
    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "03. Moving",
    "ruleNumber": "03.03",
    "summary": "A unit with multiple models stays in coherency when set up and when it finishes a move. For each model, at least one unit-mate must be within 2 inches across and 5 inches up or down. Every unit-mate must be within 9 inches across and 5 inches up or down. Use Measuring Distances for the measurement points. During End of Turn, the player controlling an out-of-coherency unit on the battlefield removes models one by one until it meets these limits. Removed models count as destroyed and do not activate rules that trigger on a model’s destruction. Under the FAQ, any models joining a unit must meet coherency with the models that unit had in play when the phase began.",
